    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d423">

                <pb facs="0661" n="559" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg559"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90H/30: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Straus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-14T19:00:00+01:00">February 14,
                            1935—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 14—4:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>129. After considerable delay, the Afghan Minister called yesterday stating that
                    he had submitted the matter of an accord to his Government which preferred a
                    formal treaty. I pointed out that the ratification of a treaty was a matter that
                    would consume considerable time and that I had assumed his interest was to
                    establish provisional relations before the setting up of a legation in Kabul
                    after which time the question of more formal relations could be studied.</p>
                <p>In my opinion, this counter-proposal need not be taken very seriously as the
                    Afghan Minister Shah Wali immediately said that if it was my opinion that such a
                    procedure would result in too great delay he would in all probability be
                    prepared to sign the accord as originally proposed.</p>
                <pb facs="0662" n="560" xml:id="pg560"/>
                <p>Unless otherwise instructed, I shall proceed at the earliest opportunity to
                    obtain his signature to the accord forwarded with the Department’s instruction
                    No. 692, January 2d, 1935, for which he has full powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Straus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
